    62	| RF-R3 — Pin before move | No module moves until RF1's characterization tests for the touched surface are green on the pre-move code. A move that needs a characterization pin to change has failed. |
    63	| RF-R4 — Move-only diffs are separate | Every move lands as a move-only commit (re-exports included) before any edit to the moved code, so reviewers can check a move without reading semantics. |
    64	| RF-R5 — Compatibility shims are inventoried | Old import paths stay importable through re-exports listed in one shim inventory, each with its retirement trigger. Re-exports do not carry monkeypatches across: every `monkeypatch` of a moved name is re-pointed at the new location in the same phase. |
    65	| RF-R6 — Source scans must not shrink | Tests that scan source text (`inspect.getsource`, reads of `cli.py`, "module stays unloaded" checks) are widened to cover each new module in the same phase. A test asserts that the scanned set covers every module it is meant to cover. |
